#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""tkreader - EPUB reader in Python + Tk, standard library only.

Opens an EPUB and shows one chapter at a time in a scrolling text view with
real fonts: headings, bold/italic, lists, quotations, code, tables, footnote
superscripts, working internal and external links, and images shown in place
(PNG and GIF natively; JPEG and other formats are converted with `sips` on
macOS or ImageMagick when one is installed).  MathML equations are typeset on
small canvases - stacked fractions, roots, stretchy brackets, matrices, limits,
accents and sub/superscripts - and inline math is set in the text itself.

Usage:  tkreader [book.epub]
        tkreader --build-app [DIR]    build a macOS tkreader.app (with icon)
        tkreader --icon-png SIZE [OUT.png]

Reading
  Space / PgDn       page down (at the end, on to the next chapter)
  Shift-Space / PgUp page up (at the top, back to the previous chapter)
  Up / Down, j / k   scroll a line        Home / End, g / G   top / bottom
  Right / n          next chapter         Left / p            previous chapter
  Alt-Left / Cmd-[   back (after following a link or choosing a contents entry)
  click a link       follow it (internal links jump; web links ask first)
View
  Ctrl/Cmd-B         show or hide the contents sidebar
  Ctrl/Cmd-+ / - / 0 larger / smaller / default text
  View menu          theme (light, sepia, dark), font, line length
Selecting
  drag, double-click (word) or triple-click (paragraph) to select; Ctrl/Cmd-C
  or the right-click menu copies (equations as TeX, images as their alt text);
  Ctrl/Cmd-A selects the whole chapter.
Search
  Ctrl/Cmd-F or /    find in the whole book; Enter / Shift-Enter next /
                     previous match (carries on into other chapters)
Other
  Ctrl/Cmd-O open a file, Ctrl/Cmd-Q quit.

The reading position of every book, and your font / theme / window choices, are
saved in ~/.tkreader.json when you quit; the last book is reopened next time.
"""

